Write a function that, given a string, returns the length of the longest palindromic subsequence within it. A subsequence is a sequence derived from the original string by deleting some or no elements without changing the order of the remaining characters. The function must be named `max_palindromic_subsequence`, accept a single string argument, and return an integer. For an empty string, return 0. The solution should have time complexity O(n^2) and space complexity O(n^2), where n is the length of the input string.

